+ALTERNATIVE TO THIS PATCH: turn GLM-5.2 MTP IndexShare off.
+
+    --json-model-override-args '{"index_share_for_mtp_iteration":false}'
+
+This patch makes the per-rank draft graph/eager decision uniform.  IndexShare-off
+instead removes the thing that makes it diverge: the guard term
+`draft_input.dsa_topk_indices is None` is seeded on the PD decode leg from
+RDMA-shipped per-request payloads (eagle_disaggregation.py:54-59), so it is a
+function of which requests each rank happens to hold -- an idle rank gets None, a
+busy one gets a tensor.  No seed, no divergence, no vote needed.
+
+Measured on 2 x 8 MI355X, GLM-5.2-MXFP4, with this patch and 02's page-table half
+BOTH asserted absent from the bytecode: 4/4 probe, 32/32 twice, 64/64, zero
+tracebacks, accept length 2.98-3.01 (no measurable cost).  It substitutes for THIS
+patch and for 02's page-table row fix; it does NOT substitute for 01 (padded rows),
+for the nextn eh_proj fix, or for 02's DP host-sync half -- those are independent
+bugs, and a host-side sync is invisible to the graph/eager decision that both this
+patch and IndexShare-off act on.
+
+Two conditions that are easy to miss: MTP must be enabled on the PREFILL leg too
+(otherwise the seed never reaches decode and the setting is untested rather than
+tested), and that arm was taken to conc=64, not 128.
+
+WHY IT IS NOT THE DEFAULT HERE: it is nearly free only because IndexShare's
+consumer is currently disabled under PD by should_use_dsa_fused_topk.  Upstream PR
+#31477 ("[Spec][PD] Enable fused TopK for GLM-5.2 MTP IndexShare") exists to remove
+that limitation; once it lands the override starts costing (~3% TPOT, reported by
+AMD's llying -- second-hand, not measured by us).  Checked with gh on 2026-07-31:
+#31477 is OPEN, reviewDecision REVIEW_REQUIRED, unmerged.  So: a good answer today
+if IndexShare is not wanted, a dated one if it is.
+
+Full arm, with anti-marker verification:
+glm52.mxfp4.spur.mooncake.packup_20260730_exp2_indexshare_off (infera.yihou.glm5.2.mxfp4)
